{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat from it na or boiled</b> — This is a commandment for all generations. All the commandments here concerning the body of the paschal offering are commandments for all generations, but the commandment concerning those who eat it — such as \"your loins girded\" (Exodus 12:11) and the blood on the lintel (Exodus 12:7) — apply only to the Passover of Egypt. Thus Scripture states concerning the second Passover (Numbers 9:11–12): \"upon unleavened bread and bitter herbs they shall eat it; they shall leave none of it until morning and shall not break a bone in it; according to all the statute of the Passover they shall make it\" — which includes roasting with fire, but not na (raw) and not boiled."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The word נא is left untranslated in its final occurrence, as Ramban is explicating the Hebrew term itself; the first instance follows the lemma verbatim."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:01.036220874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}